\tag{fdip}
\title{A supplied circle and a fixed Fourier mode}
\date{2026-10-31}

\p{How does a finite operator approximate a differential operator when
the circle and its length are already given? A periodic mesh, a
normalized pairing and a positive mass give an explicit answer for each
fixed Fourier mode. The same calculation controls one Gaussian second
moment, using [normalization](fdip-002T) and
[inverse-precision covariance](fdip-000B). The
[spatial Dirac comparison](fdip-000T) provides related finite symbols;
the scalar argument below does not require its Clifford module.}

